dant areas like forests are more  likely to house green Z orbs while  diving under water will net you plenty  of blue ones certain super attacks  feature a green icon which means that  you need to seek out additional D medals  and spend them at specified training  grounds D medals are hidden throughout  the game's massive map and a fairly  tricky to spot normally fortunately they  emanate a tell-tale aura that's only  visible when you activate your key  search which makes them less  needle-in-a-haystack and more needle  with an aura in a haystack  finally and the most innovative of  Kakarot character growth systems is the  community board as you progress through  the stories and sub stories you'll earn  soul emblems for the numerous characters  you meet assist and in some cases defeat  there are seven themed community boards  each offering different perks for  example the Z warriors community is  geared towards enhancing your prowess in  combat while the cooking community  enhances the efficacy of meals to grow  each community you'll have to place  suitable soil emblems on the board so in  the case of the Z warriors community  you'll want to be adding the likes of go  hand piccolo and krillen soul emblems  furthermore placing certain soul emblems  together triggers additional link  bonuses that will make it easier to  boost that community's rank so if you've  got even a passing knowledge of  relationships in the show you'll  definitely have an advantage you really  have grown up haven't you you look just  like Goku and he was again you can help  Goku achieve his true potential right  now because Dragon Ball Z Kakarot is  available to play on PC Xbox one and  PlayStation 4
 

